  "query_preview": "..\n(Wednesday night through Monday)\nIssued at 132 AM CDT Tue Aug 4 2026\n\nThe Long Term forecast remains unchanged. The upper-level ridge \nsettles over the Four Corners region and strengthens by the middle \nof the week. West Texas and southeast New Mexico remain on the \neastern/southeastern periphery of the ridge. As a result, highs \nacross the area remain in the mid-to-upper 90s through the weekend \n(with 100 degree temperatures confined mainly to the river valleys). \nLows settle in the mid 70s for most locations every night (60s in \nusual cool spots). Much of the area will remain dry through the \nperiod. However, disturbances rounding the edge of the ridge \n(coupled with upsloping winds) will allow for isolated showers and \nstorms to develop mainly in the higher terrain and in far western \nportions of the area during the latter half of the week.\n\nSprang",
